@startuml cue-lanes
' SPEC: _spec/apps/starchess/timeline/cue-lanes.puml
' purpose: presentation/timeline/cueLanes.ts — the cue routing registry that
' replaced id-prefix parsing. Authority: this is shipped.
!include ../../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess · Cue lanes — routing is declared, not parsed

package "presentation/timeline/cueLanes.ts" {
  component "REGISTRY: prefix → { lane, board }\nthe **only** place a cue id is read" as REG <<db>>
  component "withLane(cue)\nstamps lane · board · group" as WITH <<app>>
  component "BOARD_RUNG\npreAfterB < afterB < afterAttack < afterMove" as RUNG <<db>>
}

package "types/match.ts" {
  component "CueRouting { lane? · board? · group? }\nintersected onto every TimelineCue" as TYPE <<db>>
}

package "timelinePlayer.ts" {
  component "projectResolveTimeline\n… → ""cues.map(withLane)""" as PROJ <<app>>
  component "predicates\nisPhase1Attack · isPhase1Death · isCrushDeath\nisMoveCollisionDeath · isMineTriggerDeath\nisSimulMoveWave · isPromo* · isSpawnDeploy" as PRED <<async>>
  component "playTimeline dispatch + board ladder" as PLAY <<async>>
}

PROJ ARROW_MAIN WITH
WITH ARROW_MAIN REG
WITH ARROW_MAIN TYPE
PRED ARROW_MAIN TYPE : ""cue.lane === …""
PLAY ARROW_MAIN RUNG : advance to ""cue.board""
PLAY ARROW_MAIN PRED

note right of REG
  **Lanes** — ""gasDrop"" · ""bSpecial"" · ""deploy"" · ""crush"" ·
  ""arrivalBlast"" · ""phase1Attack"" ·
  ""phase1Death"" · ""move"" · ""collision"" · ""mineMissile"" · ""mine"" ·
  ""approach"" · ""promoWalk"" · ""promoDeploy"".

  Prefixes are matched longest-first, so ""prm"" / ""prmm"" / ""prv"" and
  ""mt"" / ""mtm"" cannot shadow each other. Ids keep their historic spelling —
  they are React keys and overlay handles now, nothing routes on them.

  **Arrival-mine cues carry the phase in the prefix**, because the same
  ""arrivalMineCues"" projector serves both ends of the resolve:
  | prefix | asked by | lane | board |
  | ""armx"" / ""armm"" / ""armd"" | ""B"" gas step · mined deploy | ""bSpecial"" | ""preAfterB"" |
  | ""farmx"" | ""F"" held mine's chase missile | ""mineMissile"" | ""afterMove"" |
  | ""farmm"" / ""farmd"" | ""F"" Extra Step · F-rank spawn arrival | ""arrivalBlast"" | ""afterMove"" |
  A held mine detonates on the marine's *real* destination, so its cues have to
  sit past the stim move on the ""afterMove"" rung — stamping them ""arm*"" would
  send a phase-4 boom back to rung 0. ""farm*"" beats the bare ""f"" move prefix by
  the longest-first rule. See ""../../../packages/starchess-core/mine-contact.puml"".
end note

note bottom
  **What it removed.** Routing was **26** ""id.startsWith(...)"" tests across
  eleven predicates, and ""isPhase1Death"" was a *deny*-list: every new cue
  prefix had to be added to it or it silently joined the wrong wave (exactly
  what the ""arm"" / ""prm"" / ""prv"" mine cues had to be hand-audited against).
  The player now contains **zero** id parsing.

  Three more things became data instead of convention:
  * **batching** — the simultaneous-move wave groups on ""cue.group"" instead of
    ""id.replace(/\\d+$/, "")"";
  * **the board ladder** — ""applyAfterB"" fires when ""BOARD_RUNG[cue.board]""
    is past ""preAfterB"", replacing the ""preAfterBSpecial"" prefix list and its
    two hand-written guards;
  * **mine snapshots** — the chase-missile handler picks ""afterMove"" vs
    ""afterAttack"" from ""cue.board"", not from a ""prmm"" prefix test.

  **The step runner shipped too.** ""runStep({ begin, beats, durationMs, end,
  next })"" owns scheduling, the ""cancelled"" re-check, cancel registration and
  the hand-off to the next cue; the nine handlers now declare only their
  patches and their extra beats (crush collapse, missile trail clear).
  ""scheduler.delay"" 30 → 20 and ""cancels.push"" 29 → 19, and a handler can no
  longer forget a leak guard.

  **Dispatch is a table.** ""run(index)"" was an eleven-branch ""if / else if""
  cascade; each branch is now a named **command** —
  ""handleGasWindow"" · ""handleDeployWindow"" · ""handlePhase1Wave"" ·
  ""handlePhase1Deaths"" · ""handleMineMissile"" · ""handleCollisionDeaths"" ·
  ""handleMineDeaths"" · ""handleMoveWave"" · ""handlePromoWalks"" ·
  ""handlePromoDeploys"" — registered in ""HANDLERS: Partial<Record<CueLane,
  CueHandler>>"" and dispatched in three lines:

  ""const handle = HANDLERS[cue.lane ?? "move"] ?? handleSequential;""

  Lanes are disjoint, so **order no longer matters** — the cascade's implicit
  precedence (deploys before phase-1, promo before the tail) was a hazard, not
  a rule. Lanes with no entry (""bSpecial"" · ""crush"" · ""approach"") fall to
  ""handleSequential"", which owns the fog-approach chains, the Tactical Jump
  and the fused lethal kingShot. Each command is now readable — and
  greppable — on its own instead of as a paragraph inside a 400-line closure.

end note
@enduml
